{
  "title": "ISSUE-25, the one remaining job: tags and compact timed in a kernel-only window (start event, launches and end event enqueued behind a blocker, so no host code runs between the events), classes that differ on the device (fixed vs random key, fixed vs random permutation) with a same-contents control of each, the SM clock read after every measurement, and a request to pin the clock at its maximum; seeds 8 and 10; the planted leak through the same window and a full-N control_null in each run",
